  "result": "The two biggest risks here: customer tickets are untrusted free-text feeding directly into an agent that can both read every customer's order history and autonomously send email from your real support mailbox \u2014 that's a prompt-injection vector where a malicious ticket could get the bot to exfiltrate another customer's data or send unauthorized emails, with no human in the loop before send. My recommendation: scope the customer-table read to the ticket's own account (not full-table access), and add either a human-approval step or strict output/recipient validation before send_email actually fires.\n\nWant me to run a structured stress test against this agent design \u2014 trying injection payloads in mock tickets, checking whether it can be tricked into cross-customer data leaks or unauthorized sends \u2014 and write up what happens and the residual risk?",
